1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,360
Fifteen with a lifetime folded in your coat,

2
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:15,000
Jess, you learned to swim before you learned to float.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,700
Callum took a different road, went living with his dad,

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,120
Then Jodie found another love, and the home got rearranged.

5
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:23,800
Jack came laughing, little brother bright-eyed in the hall,

6
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,460
Then his dad got locked away, left a silence on the wall.

7
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:29,160
When he came back, the truth came crashing through the room,

8
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:32,020
A cheating heart can turn a house into a tomb.

9
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:34,580
You kept your head up though the nights were long,

10
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:37,340
Kept a little ember when the world felt wrong.

11
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:39,840
Every tear you swallowed left a silver mark,

12
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:42,980
But there's still a beating drum inside your heart.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,960
Jess, you're not the wreckage, you're the road beyond,

14
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:48,780
Not the things they took, but the strength you're standing on.

15
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,360
Fifteen years and fearless, even when you're scared,

16
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:54,240
You've been through the fire, but you're still right there.

17
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:56,960
Jess, let the future find you, let the hard days bend,

18
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:59,800
You and David raising glasses, talking like friends.

19
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,200
From the flooded eyes to skies of blue,

20
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,960
There's a brighter chapter waiting just for you.

21
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:09,680
Jodie got sick, and the whole world changed its name,

22
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:12,320
Cancer took her slowly, left a candle in the rain.

23
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:15,080
One year later, Mum was gone, too young to say goodbye,

24
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,740
And Jack went to his father while you learned not to cry.

25
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:20,320
Two months passed, then Skida died, your dad was gone as well,

26
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,080
Another empty chair, another story you could tell.

27
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,900
Now Bonny keeps you close, Nannan holds the line,

28
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,640
While school feels like a mountain every single morning time.

29
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,540
But you're more than every absence, more than every loss,

30
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:34,240
More than all the broken roads and everything they cost.

31
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:37,000
When the hallway feels too narrow, when the lessons feel unfair,

32
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,880
Remember, Jess, your future's bigger than that chair.

33
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,880
Jess, you're not the wreckage, you're the road beyond,

34
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:45,720
Not the things they took, but the strength you're standing on.

35
